{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\nThe `verify-identity (whole-store authorship gate)` job in `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml` fetches the full `tickets` branch (`git fetch --filter=blob:none`) and fails closed if the resulting pack exceeds `REBAR_TICKETS_PACK_LIMIT_KIB` (131072 KiB = 128 MiB). As of 2026-08-04 the tickets pack measures **131830 KiB**, ~758 KiB (0.6%) over the limit, so the gate casts **Verified -1**.\n\nThis blocks EVERY Gerrit change (repo-wide), not any one change's code. First observed on change 1385 (ad85), whose own pytest/lint/typecheck jobs all pass.\n\n## Why history cannot be truncated\nThe gate deliberately mounts FULL tickets history for commit-ancestry era scoping (ADR 0051; the append-only event log is authorship-critical). So the pack only grows monotonically; compaction/truncation is not an option.\n\n## Decision (chosen approach)\nREMOVE the pack-size gate entirely (not bump the limit). Deliberate choice: the\n`REBAR_TICKETS_PACK_LIMIT_KIB` ceiling has repeatedly blocked the normal review workflow since\nthe feature was implemented, for reasons unrelated to the change under review, because the\ntickets branch is append-only full-history (ADR 0051) and its pack only ever grows — a fixed\nKiB ceiling is guaranteed to keep tripping and, once tripped, casts Verified -1 on EVERY Gerrit\nchange repo-wide. It cost far more than it protected. Change 1392 removes the env var + the\nfail-closed step and leaves an in-file NOTE recording the rationale. If tickets-pack growth\never needs bounding, use a real mechanism (server-side gc / history compaction).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The `REBAR_TICKETS_PACK_LIMIT_KIB` env var and the \"Fail closed if the filtered tickets pack exceeds its limit\" step are removed from `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml`, with an in-file NOTE documenting the deliberate removal.\n- [ ] A Gerrit change passes the `verify-identity` whole-store gate (Verified +1) without the pack-size check.\n"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785878044011153001,"uuid":"29c72fa3-e6f3-4630-8bda-298ff96afda1"}